# AI Republic Cursor Rules
# =========================
#
# Development workflow for zero-sudo, user-space native AI Republic
#
# Frontend: SwiftUI app in NeuroForgeApp/
# Backend: Python services throughout repo
# Tests:   User-space burn-in in ~/.local/share/ai-republic/

# Always use user-space paths
- AR_HOME=~/.local/share/ai-republic
- PYTHONPATH includes AR_HOME
- No sudo anywhere in runtime paths

# Build commands
- make frontend  # Build SwiftUI app
- make backend   # Start Python services
- make test      # Run burn-in tests
- make all       # Full development stack

# Test commands
- bash ~/.local/share/ai-republic/TEST_NOW.sh  # Run all tests
- ar-maint  # Maintenance mode test
- ar-spike  # Emergency spike test
- ar-status # AI Republic status

# Development workflow
1. make setup    # Initialize environment
2. make frontend # Build SwiftUI app
3. make backend  # Start services
4. make test     # Verify everything works
5. make watch    # Auto-rebuild on changes

# Emergency debugging
- If password prompts appear: pkill -f "sudo .*ai-republic"
- Check PYTHONPATH includes ~/.local/share/ai-republic
- Run: set -x; bash ~/.local/share/ai-republic/TEST_NOW.sh

# File organization
- Frontend: NeuroForgeApp/
- Backend: athena/, ai_republic/, scripts/
- Tests: ~/.local/share/ai-republic/
- Config: ~/.local/share/ai-republic/src/config_flags.py

# Key invariants
- Zero sudo in all test paths
- User-space installation only
- Environment variables over file configs
- Fallback stubs for missing dependencies
- Maintenance mode forces DRY_RUN=1
